▶ sync --git: plain files
  ✔ a note written on one computer shows up on the other, and edits travel back (7166.0452ms)
  ✔ both computers adding different notes converge to the same set (6343.8904ms)
  ✔ a second sync with nothing new changes nothing and commits nothing (3194.3954ms)
  ✔ A8: a deletion keeps the file with an archive marker; the other computer archives its copy (never deletes it), and the note does not come back (8191.0582ms)
  ✔ the same note edited on both computers: nothing is lost, the losing text is kept aside (5545.6967ms)
  ✔ --no-push commits locally and never touches the remote (1354.177ms)
  ✔ a repository with no remote is committed to locally (558.8091ms)
  ✔ a folder that is not a git repository is refused with a plain message (44.161ms)
  ✔ a missing folder is refused (0.8559ms)
  ✔ plain-text sync from a script needs --yes (it asks if the repository is private) (668.4654ms)
  ✔ --dry-run fetches, merges, writes, commits and pushes nothing (779.7053ms)
  ✔ a git-level conflict aborts cleanly and leaves the memory alone (4156.9674ms)
  ✔ only the monomem/ folder is ever committed; other files in the repository are left alone (1693.3356ms)
✔ sync --git: plain files (39699.4691ms)
▶ sync --git: encrypted
  ✔ the repository holds no readable title, text or key (1545.7656ms)
  ✔ the key stays out of the repository: a key file inside it is refused (630.7633ms)
  ✔ a second computer with a copy of the key converges; the plain text never touches the repo (2801.0517ms)
  ✔ a second computer WITHOUT the key is told so and never invents a new one over existing sealed notes (1145.1176ms)
  ✔ the wrong key stops everything before the database is changed (1152.2006ms)
  ✔ an unchanged store makes no new commit (sealed bytes are only rewritten when the text changes) (1314.9236ms)
  ✔ plain and sealed folders are never mixed in one repository (846.7498ms)
  ✔ when at-rest encryption is on, its key is reused (one key to look after) (0.3722ms)
  ✔ the work folder with readable notes is removed afterwards (925.264ms)
✔ sync --git: encrypted (10362.6932ms)
▶ sync --git: the sealed-file format
  ✔ sealing and opening round-trips; the name is bound to the path (0.5009ms)
  ✔ a sealed file renamed to another name will not open (swap protection) (0.2691ms)
  ✔ file names depend on the key, so a known note path cannot be recognised from the repository (0.1539ms)
  ✔ a different key will not open it (0.1421ms)
  ✔ paths coming out of a sealed file are checked (no .., absolute, drive letters, dot folders) (0.0928ms)
  ✔ isInside is true for children and false for siblings and parents (2.4438ms)
  ✔ isInside treats a child named ..x as inside and follows links out (2.1893ms)
  ✔ containedIn: Windows flavour (mixed separators, case, drives, 8.3 already expanded) (0.1873ms)
✔ sync --git: the sealed-file format (6.1458ms)
